    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 11,
        "line": 2,
        "text": "Those were the years after the ice caps had melted because of the greenhouse gases, and the oceans had risen to drown so many cities along all the shorelines of the world. Amsterdam. Venice. New York. Forever lost."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 11,
        "line": 651,
        "text": "That was the everlasting moment he had been waiting for. And the moment had passed, for Monica was sound asleep - more than merely asleep. Should he shake her she would never rouse. So David went to sleep too."
      }
    },
